<title>BELGIUM: Generale Bank cuts savings bond rates.</title>
<headline>Generale Bank cuts savings bond rates.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's biggest bank Generale de Banque SA said on Wednesday it would lower the interest rates offered on its &quot;cash bond&quot; savings certificates from Friday.</p>
<p>The new (old) rates are:</p>
<p>    One year  bond     3.00 pct (3.10)</p>
<p>    Two years bond     3.50 pct (3.75)</p>
<p>    Three years bond   4.10 pct (4.50)</p>
<p>    Five years bond    5.00 pct (5.45)</p>
<p>The bank said its move was a response to movements in market interest rates.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
